NOTICE — vendored engine provenance
====================================

This repository vendors the wuxing_gua judge engine, embedded byte-for-byte,
zero modification (one byte of the vendored copy differing from the source
repository is a defect; `tools/selftest.py` re-verifies the manifest).

  Vendored location   vendored/wuxing_gua/   (11 files, the judge package)
                      vendored/src/          (19 files, research modules the
                                              package imports at runtime —
                                              see vendored/wuxing_gua/__init__.py,
                                              which requires src/ as a sibling)

  Source repository   the wuxing-gua project repository (same author team;
                      desensitized: local paths not recorded here)
                      subdirectory  publish/   (its own git repository)

  Pinned version      git commit 04cf0b611f1290a5de03341d49836b4eaf139df6
                      ("explicit caliber per-element action_maps + homomorphism
                      law") HEAD of the source repo at re-vendoring time
                      (2026-11-04), working tree clean (git status verified at
                      copy time; previous pin e1b1fa86b04cba2bd0001134bf3c33255a748d39
                      of 2026-10-31 — see the re-vendoring addendum at the
                      bottom of this file)

  Package version     wuxing_gua 1.0.0 (vendored/wuxing_gua/__init__.py __version__)

  How it is run       all engine invocations run with cwd = vendored/ so that
                      `python -X utf8 -m wuxing_gua` resolves THIS copy and not
                      any site-packages install (a stale install on this
                      machine predates the n_actions relaxation and the
                      semantics-declaration layer; arbitrate.py and selftest.py
                      therefore always chdir into vendored/ before invoking it)

  Modification policy the vendored tree is frozen. Case engineering, arbitration
                      and reports in this repository MUST NOT patch the engine;
                      if the engine is wrong, the disagreement is recorded as a
                      finding, not fixed by editing the vendored copy.

  Case data provenance
                      cases/tcp/     RFC 9293 §3.3.2 Figure 5 (TCP connection
                                     state machine), transcribed edge-by-edge;
                                     base material: handoff_rewrite/output/
                                     tcp_case in the source repo, re-verified
                                     against the RFC text before adoption
                      cases/dhcp/    RFC 2131 §4.4 Figure 5 (DHCP client state
                                     machine), transcribed fresh from the RFC
                                     text for this repository
                      cases/<third>/ see that case's model.json meta and the
                                     main README

  Third-party dependency
                      networkx (arbitration column only). The engine itself is
                      zero-dependency (pure standard library) — networkx is the
                      independent juror, not a gate. Verified at selftest time.

  Authorship          The vendored wuxing_gua engine is the same authors' own
                      code (自研自用): the Symmetry Court repository and the
                      wuxing-gua engine come from the same author team, so the
                      vendoring above is a reuse of self-owned code, not an
                      import of outside work. The engine carries its own MIT
                      license (Copyright (c) 2026 wuxing-gua contributors),
                      compatible with the MIT license of this repository; the
                      engine's license terms continue to govern the vendored
                      copy itself.

